KONOHA MEDICAL CORPS — CHAKRA RESERVE ASSESSMENT

Purpose: baseline measurement of a shinobi's chakra capacity, control, and recovery rate for mission-readiness.

Assessment notes (representative):
- Uzumaki, Naruto — Exceptionally large reserves (well above genin norm), attributed to Uzumaki lineage and sealed tenant. Chakra CONTROL rated poor at baseline; improving with tree-walking and water-walking exercises.
- Haruno, Sakura — Reserves modest; chakra CONTROL rated excellent. Strong candidate for medical-nin training.
- Uchiha, Sasuke — Reserves above average; control good.
- Hyuga, Neji — Precise control consistent with Gentle Fist chakra-point work.

Recommendation: pair large-reserve/low-control shinobi with control drills before elemental training. Refer high-control candidates to the Medical Corps.

Assessed by Konoha Hospital, Chakra Metrics Division.
